#: CONTEXT-MAP.md
msgid "Context map"
msgstr ""

#: CONTEXT-MAP.md
msgid "We divide the EMIS domain into bounded contexts. Each context has its own language, one steward who owns it, and its own catalogs. A context talks to the others only through interfaces it publishes. You'll find how the contexts are designed, with their subdomains, aggregates, invariants and events, in the [domain design]{1}. Terms about the blueprint and the platform itself are in the [glossary]{2}."
msgstr ""

#: CONTEXT-MAP.md
msgid "Contexts"
msgstr ""

#: CONTEXT-MAP.md
msgid "[Reference]{1} is the shared kernel of time, codes, geography and registries."
msgstr ""

#: CONTEXT-MAP.md
msgid "[People]{1} records each person once, whatever roles they hold."
msgstr ""

#: CONTEXT-MAP.md
msgid "[Institutions]{1} covers institutions, the sites they occupy and the state of those sites."
msgstr ""

#: CONTEXT-MAP.md
msgid "[Learning]{1} covers enrolment, class membership, attendance, progression and guardianship."
msgstr ""

#: CONTEXT-MAP.md
msgid "[Workforce]{1} covers posts and the staff posted to them."
msgstr ""

#: CONTEXT-MAP.md
msgid "[Curriculum]{1} covers programmes, grades, subjects and classes."
msgstr ""

#: CONTEXT-MAP.md
msgid "[Assessment]{1} covers tests and examinations, their candidates and their results."
msgstr ""

#: CONTEXT-MAP.md
msgid "[Statistics]{1} covers collections, returns, snapshots, indicators and publication."
msgstr ""

#: CONTEXT-MAP.md
msgid "[Records]{1} covers retention, disposal, correction and individual disclosure."
msgstr ""

#: CONTEXT-MAP.md
msgid "[Operations]{1} covers budgets, assets, entitlement schemes and safety."
msgstr ""

#: CONTEXT-MAP.md
msgid "Relationships"
msgstr ""

#: CONTEXT-MAP.md
msgid "Each relationship below is named after the pattern it follows."
msgstr ""

#: CONTEXT-MAP.md
msgid "**Reference → every context** is a shared kernel. Every context uses code lists, academic periods, reference dates and administrative areas unchanged, so every steward reviews a change to them."
msgstr ""

#: CONTEXT-MAP.md
msgid "**External registers → People** goes through an anti-corruption layer. People reads civil and other registers through an adapter, which translates their identifiers and outcomes into People's language. Their model never leaks in."
msgstr ""

#: CONTEXT-MAP.md
msgid "**People → Learning, Workforce, Records** is an open host service with a published language. People publishes a registry interface keyed by the person identifier. The other contexts hold only that identifier, never a copy of the person."
msgstr ""

#: CONTEXT-MAP.md
msgid "**Institutions → Learning, Workforce, Statistics, Operations** is an open host service. Other contexts read the institution registry by identifier, and occupancy tells them which sites an institution uses."
msgstr ""

#: CONTEXT-MAP.md
msgid "**Curriculum → Learning, Assessment** is a customer and supplier relationship. Learning and Assessment need programmes, grades and subjects, so Curriculum agrees changes with them before releasing them."
msgstr ""

#: CONTEXT-MAP.md
msgid "**Learning ↔ Workforce** is a partnership through assignments. A teacher teaches a class, and each context owns its own side of that: class membership in Learning, the assignment in Workforce. So the two change together."
msgstr ""

#: CONTEXT-MAP.md
msgid "**Learning, Workforce, Institutions, Assessment → Statistics** is a published language. Statistics reads only the counts that each context publishes to gold, as at a reference date, together with the semantic layer's definitions over them. It never reads their operational records."
msgstr ""

#: CONTEXT-MAP.md
msgid "**Statistics → international bodies** is a published language too, in the formats those bodies define, such as SDMX and the UIS questionnaires."
msgstr ""

#: CONTEXT-MAP.md
msgid "**Records → every context** is a conformist relationship. Records sets the retention, disposal and disclosure rules once, and every context applies them unchanged to the records it owns."
msgstr ""

#: CONTEXT-MAP.md
msgid "**Other government systems ↔ Workforce, Operations** goes through an anti-corruption layer. Exchanges run through declared feeds that translate in both directions."
msgstr ""
